<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1891"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:raolesin@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Ryan_olesin<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ryan_olesin<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 14, 2004 - 6:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ve been noticing alot of reruns now, and what better case to cover.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1891-->
<!--Post: 1892--><!--Time: 1103078411-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1892"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 14, 2004 - 6:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree, Ryan. <i>Cold Case Files</i> did an awesome job with their Zodiac episode from 2003 and I&#39;d expect the same if they decide to tackle BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1892-->
<!--Post: 1894--><!--Time: 1103079496-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1894"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Screamer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Screamer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, December 14, 2004 - 6:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I contacted Cold Case Files a month or two after BTK resurfaced to suggest an episode. I know that they covered Zodiac, why not BTK? I have yet to hear anything. <BR> <BR>I also noticed that after I suggested it, Bill Kurtis now says at the end of the show, &#34;Do you know of any &#34;SOLVED&#34; cold cases, we&#39;d like to hear from you&#34;. It might have always said &#34;solved&#34;, maybe I&#39;m mistaken. <BR> <BR>I also find it interesting that Bill Kurtis, is from Kansas and he was back there to pick up an award or something. I think that he even has a ranch there. <BR> <BR>I sure wish that they would pick up the story.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1894-->
<!--Post: 3151--><!--Time: 1104517861-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3151"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 10:31 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Cold Case files have always been ones that have been solved.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3151-->
<!--Post: 3155--><!--Time: 1104526269-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3155"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 12:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Not always, Tornado.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3155-->
<!--Post: 3425--><!--Time: 1104888602-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3425"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Weeza<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Weeza<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 5:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->nope Tornado, they&#39;ve featured several unsolved cases. Two that come to mind are &#34;Precious Doe&#34; and of course &#34;Zodiac&#34;. <BR>Yes the majority are solved cases, but they are open to unsolved cases as well.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3425-->
<!--Post: 3426--><!--Time: 1104888842-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3426"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Weeza<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Weeza<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 5:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I also noticed that after I suggested it, Bill Kurtis now says at the end of the show, &#34;Do you know of any &#34;SOLVED&#34; cold cases, we&#39;d like to hear from you&#34;. It might have always said &#34;solved&#34;, maybe I&#39;m mistaken. <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR>OKAY, so how many years ago did you suggest this, because Mr. Kurtis has used that phrase and request for cases for YEARS now. Don&#39;t believe me? You can order copies of the past episodes on their website. <BR>Unless you wrote to him and suggested it from their first episode, I hihly doubt you were the inspiration. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3426-->
<!--Post: 3645--><!--Time: 1105079844-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3645"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Screamer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Screamer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 10:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Weeza, <BR> <BR>As I said in my post, &#34;It might have always said &#34;solved&#34;, maybe I&#39;m mistaken&#34;. I believe you, no need for me to order copies to prove it to myself. That wasn&#39;t the point. Trust me, I&#39;m not trying to take credit for being the inspiration. I knew that they looked at unsolved cases, I just found it odd one night. <BR> <BR>Peace.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3645-->
